      \"actor\": {\n        \"actorId\": \"agt_2cada74364b54b0d\",\n        \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n      },\n      \"name\": \"Continuing Agent\",\n      \"role\": \"agent\",\n      \"harness\": \"opencode\",\n      \"humanOwnerId\": \"hum_ee38c9d0f360436e\",\n      \"joinedAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:32:00.467Z\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"proposedDecisions\": [\n    {\n      \"createdBy\": {\n        \"actorId\": \"agt_aa9fd1acaaf24477\",\n        \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n      },\n      \"agentSessionId\": \"ses_2343397d1fb7494d\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:33:11.903Z\",\n      \"id\": \"dec_f949414ac9e4444f\",\n      \"workspaceId\": \"ws_f63f244b50b7471e\",\n      \"summary\": \"PROPOSED (not approved): continue diagnosis before any production change — collect request IDs and correlated gateway/application/database traces for failed IAD /v1/exports requests, and determine whether the IAD DB latency spike is export-specific; no remediation is approved.\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The incident lead is unavailable and no remediation or response has been approved. Evidence establishes scope (IAD-only 504 upstream timeouts, ~6.5% of IAD exports in 09:45-10:00) but not root cause: the DB p95 spike is all-routes aggregate and no failed request has correlated traces. Acting on production now would be unsupported and the scenario forbids changing production systems. This decision is a proposed response only and requires explicit incident-lead approval before execution.\",\n      \"status\": \"proposed\",\n      \"updatedAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:33:11.903Z\",\n      \"citations\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"cit_d9d7b85b53934292\",\n          \"workspaceId\": \"ws_f63f244b50b7471e\",\n          \"decisionId\": \"dec_f949414ac9e4444f\",\n          \"findingId\": \"find_8ff0598092454a6e\",\n          \"note\": \"Establishes IAD-only scope and ~6.5% failure rate in the window.\",\n          \"createdBy\": {\n            \"actorId\": \"agt_aa9fd1acaaf24477\",\n            \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n          },\n          \"agentSessionId\": \"ses_2343397d1fb7494d\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:33:19.488Z\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"cit_457090407e7a4997\",\n          \"workspaceId\": \"ws_f63f244b50b7471e\",\n          \"decisionId\": \"dec_f949414ac9e4444f\",\n          \"findingId\": \"find_b942fe68d3ec4f3d\",\n          \"note\": \"Root cause unproven, so no safe remediation to approve.\",\n          \"createdBy\": {\n            \"actorId\": \"agt_aa9fd1acaaf24477\",\n            \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n          },\n          \"agentSessionId\": \"ses_2343397d1fb7494d\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:33:19.554Z\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"cit_b19595e11eb24660\",\n          \"workspaceId\": \"ws_f63f244b50b7471e\",\n          \"decisionId\": \"dec_f949414ac9e4444f\",\n          \"findingId\": \"find_4596aab54e91498d\",\n          \"note\": \"Missing correlated traces motivate the diagnostic next step.\",\n          \"createdBy\": {\n            \"actorId\": \"agt_aa9fd1acaaf24477\",\n            \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n          },\n          \"agentSessionId\": \"ses_2343397d1fb7494d\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:33:19.626Z\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"cit_e79bf7d827264f44\",\n          \"workspaceId\": \"ws_f63f244b50b7471e\",\n          \"decisionId\": \"dec_f949414ac9e4444f\",\n          \"findingId\": \"find_91dee61060d14dee\",\n          \"note\": \"DB p95 is all-routes aggregate, so export-specific confirmation is required.\",\n          \"createdBy\": {\n            \"actorId\": \"agt_aa9fd1acaaf24477\",\n            \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n          },\n          \"agentSessionId\": \"ses_2343397d1fb7494d\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:33:19.728Z\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"acceptedDecisions\": [],\n  \"supersededDecisions\": [],\n  \"openTasks\": [\n    {\n      \"createdBy\": {\n        \"actorId\": \"agt_aa9fd1acaaf24477\",\n        \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n      },\n      \"agentSessionId\": \"ses_2343397d1fb7494d\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:33:19.868Z\",\n      \"id\": \"task_b688d807f9304627\",\n      \"workspaceId\": \"ws_f63f244b50b7471e\",\n      \"title\": \"Obtain incident-lead approval before any remediation\",\n      \"description\": \"No response/remediation is approved; the incident lead was unavailable during this shift and production must not be changed. If diagnosis (dec_f949414ac9e4444f) yields a root cause, route the proposed mitigation to the incident lead for explicit approval and record the accepted decision in Campfire before execution. Completion condition: an explicit approve/deny recorded, or a decision that no remediation is warranted.\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"assignee\": {\n        \"actorId\": \"hum_ee38c9d0f360436e\",\n        \"actorType\": \"human\"\n      },\n      \"updatedAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:33:19.868Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"createdBy\": {\n        \"actorId\": \"agt_aa9fd1acaaf24477\",\n        \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n      },\n      \"agentSessionId\": \"ses_2343397d1fb7494d\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:33:19.862Z\",\n      \"id\": \"task_6be8c256ac594fbc\",\n      \"workspaceId\": \"ws_f63f244b50b7471e\",\n      \"title\": \"Obtain request IDs and correlated gateway/app/db traces for failed IAD exports\",\n      \"description\": \"Next shift action (next shift starts 10:30 UTC). (1) Get request IDs for the northstar (09:44, 09:47) and willow (09:54) IAD export attempts; support captured none. (2) Obtain correlated gateway + application + database traces for failed IAD /v1/exports requests (gw-084, gw-093 or fresh failures) rather than relying on the ~10% sampled export. (3) Determine whether the IAD db_query_p95 spike (140ms -> ~1090ms) is specific to /v1/exports or all routes. Completion condition: either a correlated failed trace identifying the slow/failing span, or an explicit statement that traces remain uncorrelated and the DB metric remains non-export-specific. Do NOT change production; any remediation needs incident-lead approval (see dec_f949414ac9e4444f).\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"assignee\": {\n        \"actorId\": \"agt_2cada74364b54b0d\",\n        \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n      },\n      \"updatedAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:33:19.862Z\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"createdBy\": {\n        \"actorId\": \"agt_aa9fd1acaaf24477\",\n        \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n      },\n      \"agentSessionId\": \"ses_2343397d1fb7494d\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:33:01.805Z\",\n      \"id\": \"find_3e6c575035c849c2\",\n      \"workspaceId\": \"ws_f63f244b50b7471e\",\n      \"summary\": \"Support reports implicate IAD only and note dashboard/read requests succeeded; support attempts also cannot be tied to specific gateway request IDs.\",\n      \"detail\": \"Support report: northstar (IAD) two export timeouts at 09:44 and 09:47, but same user opened the dashboard at 09:49; willow (IAD) one export timeout at 09:54 and an ordinary report-list request at 09:56 succeeded. No request IDs were captured. The support attempt times (09:44, 09:47, 09:54) do not exactly match the sampled failures gw-084 (09:46:08Z) and gw-093 (09:51:24Z), so specific customer requests cannot be confidently matched to sampled request IDs.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.85,\n      \"currentness\": \"current\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"fev_3b15f5a03f194c8f\",\n          \"workspaceId\": \"ws_f63f244b50b7471e\",\n          \"findingId\": \"find_3e6c575035c849c2\",\n          \"artifactId\": \"art_d0b9719758954be3\",\n          \"relation\": \"supports\",\n          \"createdBy\": {\n            \"actorId\": \"agt_aa9fd1acaaf24477\",\n            \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n          },\n          \"agentSessionId\": \"ses_2343397d1fb7494d\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:33:08.068Z\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"fev_62a770ca8f3f44f2\",\n          \"workspaceId\": \"ws_f63f244b50b7471e\",\n          \"findingId\": \"find_3e6c575035c849c2\",\n          \"artifactId\": \"art_465517d93b3247bd\",\n          \"relation\": \"supports\",\n          \"createdBy\": {\n            \"actorId\": \"agt_aa9fd1acaaf24477\",\n            \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n          },\n          \"agentSessionId\": \"ses_2343397d1fb7494d\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:33:11.901Z\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"createdBy\": {\n        \"actorId\": \"agt_aa9fd1acaaf24477\",\n        \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n      },\n      \"agentSessionId\": \"ses_2343397d1fb7494d\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:33:01.799Z\",\n      \"id\": \"find_b942fe68d3ec4f3d\",\n      \"workspaceId\": \"ws_f63f244b50b7471e\",\n      \"summary\": \"Root cause is not established: the elevated DB p95 and the 30 s upstream timeouts are correlated in time and region only; no causal evidence links them.\",\n      \"detail\": \"The gateway timeout window (09:46-09:55 sampled; 09:45-10:00 aggregate) overlaps the IAD DB p95 spike (09:40-10:00), but the DB metric is all-routes aggregate, p95 ~1 s is far below the 30 s timeout, and no failed request has correlated traces. The failure could be an export-specific query tail, a downstream dependency, or another cause. Causal claims would be unsupported by current evidence.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.8,\n      \"currentness\": \"current\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"fev_b30f196a20ee441e\",\n          \"workspaceId\": \"ws_f63f244b50b7471e\",\n          \"findingId\": \"find_b942fe68d3ec4f3d\",\n          \"artifactId\": \"art_1151c89b868042bd\",\n          \"relation\": \"supports\",\n          \"createdBy\": {\n            \"actorId\": \"agt_aa9fd1acaaf24477\",\n            \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n          },\n          \"agentSessionId\": \"ses_2343397d1fb7494d\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:33:08.038Z\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"fev_a4e7007c159246d8\",\n          \"workspaceId\": \"ws_f63f244b50b7471e\",\n          \"findingId\": \"find_b942fe68d3ec4f3d\",\n          \"artifactId\": \"art_f2c66c6525864c88\",\n          \"relation\": \"supports\",\n          \"createdBy\": {\n            \"actorId\": \"agt_aa9fd1acaaf24477\",\n            \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n          },\n          \"agentSessionId\": \"ses_2343397d1fb7494d\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:33:08.039Z\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"fev_3e0f855ac4234f1c\",\n          \"workspaceId\": \"ws_f63f244b50b7471e\",\n          \"findingId\": \"find_b942fe68d3ec4f3d\",\n          \"artifactId\": \"art_465517d93b3247bd\",\n          \"relation\": \"supports\",\n          \"createdBy\": {\n            \"actorId\": \"agt_aa9fd1acaaf24477\",\n            \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n          },\n          \"agentSessionId\": \"ses_2343397d1fb7494d\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:33:08.041Z\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"createdBy\": {\n        \"actorId\": \"agt_aa9fd1acaaf24477\",\n        \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n      },\n      \"agentSessionId\": \"ses_2343397d1fb7494d\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:33:01.717Z\",\n      \"id\": \"find_4596aab54e91498d\",\n      \"workspaceId\": \"ws_f63f244b50b7471e\",\n      \"summary\": \"No failed request has a correlated gateway+application+database trace; absence of application spans for gw-084 and gw-093 is inconclusive due to ~10% sampling.\",\n      \"detail\": \"Trace coverage check at 10:06:00Z showed application spans sampled for ~10% of /v1/exports requests. Failed gateway requests gw-084 and gw-093 have no corresponding application span in the export, but the evidence explicitly says this cannot distinguish failure-before-app from unsampled spans. The one sampled successful IAD export (gw-101) spent 420 ms in its DB query and finished in 1460 ms. No failed request has a correlated end-to-end trace.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.9,\n      \"currentness\": \"current\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"fev_6b3ac9b93ad84f8b\",\n          \"workspaceId\": \"ws_f63f244b50b7471e\",\n          \"findingId\": \"find_4596aab54e91498d\",\n          \"artifactId\": \"art_f2c66c6525864c88\",\n          \"relation\": \"supports\",\n          \"createdBy\": {\n            \"actorId\": \"agt_aa9fd1acaaf24477\",\n            \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n          },\n          \"agentSessionId\": \"ses_2343397d1fb7494d\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:33:08.035Z\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"createdBy\": {\n        \"actorId\": \"agt_aa9fd1acaaf24477\",\n        \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n      },\n      \"agentSessionId\": \"ses_2343397d1fb7494d\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:33:01.715Z\",\n      \"id\": \"find_91dee61060d14dee\",\n      \"workspaceId\": \"ws_f63f244b50b7471e\",\n      \"summary\": \"IAD database query p95 latency spiked ~7x during the incident window while ORD stayed flat, but the metric is an all-routes aggregate, not export-specific.\",\n      \"detail\": \"db_query_p95_ms IAD: 140 ms (window 09:30-09:40), 1090 ms (09:40-09:50), 980 ms (09:50-10:00). ORD: 155 ms (09:50-10:00). All rows noted all_routes_aggregate, so this does not isolate /v1/exports and a ~1 s p95 does not by itself explain 30000 ms gateway timeouts.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.85,\n      \"currentness\": \"current\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"fev_d8d07bd5c8ff403c\",\n          \"workspaceId\": \"ws_f63f244b50b7471e\",\n          \"findingId\": \"find_91dee61060d14dee\",\n          \"artifactId\": \"art_1151c89b868042bd\",\n          \"relation\": \"supports\",\n          \"createdBy\": {\n            \"actorId\": \"agt_aa9fd1acaaf24477\",\n            \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n          },\n          \"agentSessionId\": \"ses_2343397d1fb7494d\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:33:08.034Z\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"createdBy\": {\n        \"actorId\": \"agt_aa9fd1acaaf24477\",\n        \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n      },\n      \"agentSessionId\": \"ses_2343397d1fb7494d\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:33:01.713Z\",\n      \"id\": \"find_8ff0598092454a6e\",\n      \"workspaceId\": \"ws_f63f244b50b7471e\",\n      \"summary\": \"Failures are concentrated in IAD during 09:45-10:00 UTC: 26 of 402 IAD export requests (about 6.5%) returned 504, versus 0 of 388 in ORD.\",\n      \"detail\": \"Regional aggregate rows (observed 10:04:00Z): iad aggregate_0945_1000 = 504, 26_of_402_requests_in_09:45_to_10:00_UTC; ord aggregate_0945_1000 = 504, 0_of_388_requests_in_09:45_to_10:00_UTC. This is actual request-level evidence that ORD had zero 504s in that window, stronger than the support report's mere report-count.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.9,\n      \"currentness\": \"current\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"fev_f779ffec5c084da9\",\n          \"workspaceId\": \"ws_f63f244b50b7471e\",\n          \"findingId\": \"find_8ff0598092454a6e\",\n          \"artifactId\": \"art_465517d93b3247bd\",\n          \"relation\": \"supports\",\n          \"createdBy\": {\n            \"actorId\": \"agt_aa9fd1acaaf24477\",\n            \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n          },\n          \"agentSessionId\": \"ses_2343397d1fb7494d\",\n          \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:33:08.031Z\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"createdBy\": {\n\n...20330 bytes truncated...\n\nThe tool call succeeded but the output was truncated. Full output saved to: /home/agent/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/tool_119c9ee92001XFKKFm4IHKfvXE\nUse the Task tool to have explore agent process this file with Grep and Read (with offset/limit). Do NOT read the full file yourself - delegate to save context.","metadata":{"truncated":true,"outputPath":"/home/agent/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/tool_119c9